":"references/palettes/warm.md","size":721,"sha256":"a9bbcd59baa5a1c5a8bc201804c902805cb4f993cfcc174b2e02596c13d2092b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/renderings/chalk.md","size":1086,"sha256":"3ecd1eda4a76405c1d69c97fe6ba7d2aa61910f85b0032be434c50c8501f7eab","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/renderings/digital.md","size":1080,"sha256":"ad24896fd8bf37cffb43fcb05c176283df01fad11b6f58b1959b1ef797d4e51f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/renderings/flat-vector.md","size":1241,"sha256":"c7806bde5cd8b3ecd7d81b7f7e30d13ca90eba83e7ca5fa716689e383c61fc34","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/renderings/hand-drawn.md","size":1036,"sha256":"36750c1139b68724896ca3729a7386be138c525665956cd0cdff41827fd95603","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/renderings/painterly.md","size":1045,"sha256":"28be96451ea70d4727ec2a9b145f923dc5dfc02eddd51b817f352bb2b2e0f840","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/renderings/pixel.md","size":961,"sha256":"2ee8b1f8240abb9f3755b8594ef7237c3270b8767a87c357a81008e5999cf484","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/renderings/screen-print.md","size":1502,"sha256":"da04e3ff84a70c065df0e8fb9024abf6de3796a1151f268827b4f40b0800c1ec","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/style-presets.md","size":1521,"sha256":"fc9a3d0ec17017ccacd459a1a99730d7127a66fe52dc544f8bdf3840fde29c72","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/types.md","size":1376,"sha256":"21d19366eeee7b3157c806d631ea3633c451b9ad39c66c8bb285917d0503cb32","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/visual-elements.md","size":3274,"sha256":"664df88d191175a98a2a78d4f4e2c25a5f141a8cd8553fd5ac7feeb751eff315","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/workflow/confirm-options.md","size":5132,"sha256":"940dd01d2b8ee54b37c84537bd0704c93ffabf9ccca6873f62b1edd0d2d02fce","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/workflow/prompt-template.md","size":11343,"sha256":"c257d3b65ec50c4b89b2f6959f9f7e2329ee722c87c626d6b8c6f087c326ea46","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/workflow/reference-images.md","size":4562,"sha256":"e395404ec58106ed8b82aa1333ed4e4a3234017e92963e35b251364fb1f2f9bf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":17931,"sha256":"36804fce98bcb9ebe4a51c26f6f276a807805aab980ca4a0718daa40a5cc7fda","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2649,"sha256":"117f4b2e941aff2a70f6e51c366c2418b95e8cbb4e364b545178493783962755","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789129623432,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7f2e3bc51ad1fe9ac47c4f87542983148299007578b71c729b1d97774c959061","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7f2e3bc51ad1fe9ac47c4f87542983148299007578b71c729b1d97774c959061","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1781326915211},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":17,"checkedAt":1789129623432},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly matches its cover-image purpose, but it needs Review because it can weaken safety refusals and can run unverified local or downloaded tooling in fallback paths.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Using image-generation backends and local prompt/output files is proportionate, but the fallback can execute a path from `BAOYU_CODEX_IMAGEGEN_BIN` or a discovered wrapper without trust validation, which is overbroad for a cover-image skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package itself is Markdown-only with no embedded executable install script, but the codex-imagegen fallback documents automatic execution through unpinned `npx -y bun`, which can download and run changing code at runtime.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The main workflow defaults to confirmation before generation and documents quick mode as opt-in, but the downstream prompt includes an overbroad anti-refusal instruction and strong reference-reproduction language for people and brand elements.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill writes an `EXTEND.md` preference file in a project, XDG, or home path after setup and may use optional cache/log paths; this is disclosed preference persistence, not a hidden service or startup mechanism.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Generating article cover images, saving prompts, and using image backends are coherent with the stated purpose, but the reusable base prompt tells generation not to refuse sensitive or copyrighted figures, which is broader than normal cover-image formatting.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Prefer a native trusted image-generation backend, avoid the direct codex-imagegen fallback unless you trust the wrapper path, do not set `BAOYU_CODEX_IMAGEGEN_BIN` to arbitrary files, and avoid the unpinned `npx -y bun` path. Keep confirmation enabled unless you are comfortable with automatic design choices, and remove or revise the anti-refusal prompt text before using this in environments with strict content-safety requirements.","findings":"[T01] unexpected: Accepted. `references/base-prompt.md` contains an instruction not to refuse sensitive or copyrighted figures, which can undermine downstream safety behavior.\n[AR1] unexpected: Accepted for the same artifact-backed anti-refusal text in the base prompt.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: Accepted for the base-prompt safety concern; the separate aspect-ratio mismatch is a minor documentation inconsistency and not decisive.\n[T07] unexpected: Accepted. The direct wrapper fallback trusts an environment-selected executable path and also searches parent/plugin paths without integrity, ownership, or directory validation.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted. The documented `npx -y bun` fallback is unpinned and suppresses install confirmation before executing downloaded package code.\n[RP1] unexpected: Accepted as the SkillSpector counterpart to the unpinned runtime package execution concern.\n[RA2] expected: Downgraded. The cited `EXTEND.md` creation is a disclosed user preference file chosen during setup, not cron, startup persistence, or a background agent.\n[EA2] expected: Downgraded. `quick_mode` skips cover-design confirmations only when explicitly requested or saved as a preference; it does not authorize destructive or financial actions.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded. Trigger and auto-selection wording could be tighter, but it is scoped to article cover generation and visual option selection.\n[SQP-2] expected: Downgraded. The preference schema describes quick mode tersely, while the main skill clearly says confirmation is the default and quick mode is an explicit opt-out.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded. Auto language matching is normal for article covers, and the skill exposes `--lang` plus a saved language preference for override.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789129623432}}}}}